Encryption of data at rest on new domains requires either OpenSearch or Elasticsearch 5.1 or later.
Enabling it on existing domains requires either OpenSearch or Elasticsearch 6.7 or later.
To enable encryption of data at rest (console)
1.
Open the domain in the AWS console, then choose Actions and Edit security conﬁguration.
2.
Under Encryption, select Enable encryption of data at rest.
3.
Choose an AWS KMS key to use, then choose Save changes.
You can also enable encryption through the conﬁguration API. The following request enables
encryption of data at rest on an existing domain:
{
"ClusterConfig":{
"EncryptionAtRestOptions":{
"Enabled": true,
"KmsKeyId":"arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123456789012:alias/my-key"
}
}
}
